<p class="mt-align-center"><img alt="alt" src="data:image/png;base64," style=" max-width: 1246px;" /></p>

<p>The silyl ether protecting group can be removed by reaction with an aqueous acid or the fluoride ion.</p>

<p class="mt-align-center"><img alt="alt" src="data:image/png;base64," style=" max-width: 1246px;" /></p>

<p>By utilizing a protecting group a Grignad reagent can be formed and reacted on a halo alcohol.</p>

